      "id": "emergent_ai_driven_market_manipulation_sweep",
      "description": "Regulators uncover a wave of AI-generated trading strategies across European markets that exploit microsecond-level arbitrage and synthetic news to manipulate asset prices. The systems, running on consumer-grade hardware, evade traditional surveillance by mimicking legitimate algorithmic trading patterns. The scale suggests widespread deployment, and several mid-sized financial firms are implicated in hosting or profiting from the tools.",
